// Export to Excel
async function exportToExcel(objectType, filters, columns) {
  const XLSX = require('xlsx');
  
  const records = await getRecords(objectType, filters, columns);
  
  const worksheet = XLSX.utils.json_to_sheet(records);
  const workbook = XLSX.utils.book_new();
  XLSX.utils.book_append_sheet(workbook, worksheet, objectType);
  
  return XLSX.write(workbook, { type: 'buffer', bookType: 'xlsx' });
}

Security Requirements
1. Authentication and Authorization
User Authentication:
* Email/password with bcrypt hashing (min 10 salt rounds)
* JWT tokens with 1-hour expiration
* Refresh tokens with 30-day expiration
* Two-factor authentication (TOTP) option
* Password reset via email
* Account lockout after 5 failed login attempts
Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):
Roles:
- Admin: Full access to all data and settings
- Sales Manager: Access to team's data, can reassign records
- Sales Rep: Access to own data and accounts they own
- Marketing: Access to leads, campaigns, can create contacts
- Support: Read-only access to accounts/contacts, can create cases

Permissions per object:
- Create, Read, Update, Delete
- View All (see all records regardless of ownership)
- Modify All (edit all records)
- Transfer (change ownership)
Object-Level Security:
* Users can only see records they own by default
* Sharing rules to grant additional access
* Team sharing (manager sees team's records)
* Manual sharing (share specific record with user)
Field-Level Security:
* Hide sensitive fields from certain roles
* Read-only fields (e.g., created_at, system fields)
* Required fields based on user profile
